  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Women are Smarter** (1 review): Reviewer found the opener a perfect choice supporting women, hitting home emotionally and urging men to listen to and respect women [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Women are Smarter**: rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n- **Dark Star V.1**: back after 143 archived shows (1820 days); rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **Dear Mr. Fantasy/Hey Jude finale**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Sing Me Back Home**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **Mickey**: rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n- **All Blues**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **dac2022-06-24.AKGmix.toaste.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 204 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the recording captures the show's tenor and tone well [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The band expressed support for women's rights through music and visuals, the day the Supreme Court undid 50 years of progress [1]\n- Chatting audience members seemingly miss out on the band's music, according to the reviewer [2]\n- Crowd had talkers, chompers and casual fans; reviewer's YouTube samples drew similar complaints [3]\n- Reviewer heard homage to jazz artists like Miles, Trane, Pharoh Sanders and Branford, plus many covers and teases [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dac2022-06-24.AKGmix.toaste.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: 3x AKG398 shotguns (L,C,R); 1x AKG394 Figure-8 (L,R); 2x AKG391 cardioids ortf (L,R); 2x AKG392 omnis 2-foot spread (L,R) > Zoom F8 @ 44.1/16 [1]. Also: Recorded from the taper section OTS, rear of Field-X, around shortstop [1]",
